@* The reader's own status, beside the publication status the sources supply. They are
   two separate fields in the model and two separate readings of the same series
   (CLAUDE.md — Series status vs Publication status), so the hero states both rather
   than blending them into one word.

   A dropdown rather than the segmented control the view toggles use: four word-length
   segments is a third of the hero's meta row, and this is a choice made rarely — it
   should be readable at rest and cheap to reach, not permanently laid out. *@

<span class="tracking">
    <span class="tracking__label">Tracking</span>
    <Dropdown Options="StatusOptions"
              Value="@Series.TrackingStatus.ToString()"
              ValueChanged="OnChosenAsync"
              Disabled="SeriesState.IsSaving"
              AriaLabel="How you are tracking this series" />
</span>
